Z||000003||JohnnyK||02-20-2001||11:40 PM||||I don't want to buy anything, I want to tighten the mounts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I thought there would be more than one engine mount though (Can't be the tranny mounts, as I just put a new clutch in).||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||02-21-2001||09:39 PM||||If they were loose, that would mean that the bolt holding the mount bracket to the cradle and everything would phsically have to have worked its nut loose and probably would have come off by now.  So, those "tards" that you were talking about probably saw that the engine could move around a little bit, and said they were loose, when in fact, a worn mount bushing would do this.  Poly bushings will last you, but they can be a little bit on the harsh side, as for transmitting vibration from the engine to the rest of the car.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||2
Z||000005||JohnnyK||02-21-2001||11:45 PM||||I specifically said "worn?" and they said "Nope, just loose". Maybe I should look into this. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gold-86SE||02-22-2001||10:17 AM||||<BR>As c m west stated previously, there are three mounts. Two on the transmission and one on the drivebelt side of the engine.<P>All you should need is a 13mm and 15mm sockets, and wrenches to tighten them down.  I don't use a torque wrench, I just make them nice and tight.<P>You will have to raise and then support the Fiero on stands to tighten the mounts.<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
